# Notifications (LWS 1.0 core section 10).
"@context":
  - ../context.jsonld
  - ../touchstone.jsonld
id: "#manifest"
type: Manifest
label: "LWS 1.0 core: notifications"
comment: >-
  A storage MAY support notifications. Defined here: discovery, and creating a
  subscription (request and response fields, and the subscribe-time authorization MUST).
  The subscription tests use WebhookSubscription, the one subscription type with a
  defined request shape, and apply only where it is advertised. Delivery is not yet
  defined: it needs a sink the target can reach, and its authorization MUSTs deserve a
  negative matrix of their own. See README.md, "Not yet defined".
specification:
  - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/
entries:

  - id: "#notification-service-advertised"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: notification-service-advertised
    label: A storage that supports notifications advertises a well-formed NotificationService
    comment: >-
      Support is optional, so a description without a NotificationService makes the
      test inapplicable. One that has it must give the service a serviceEndpoint and a
      subscriptionType array of strings.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#notification-discovery
    traits: [Get, Discovery, Notifications, StorageDescription]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/notifications-advertise-notificationservice
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/notificationservice-endpoint-and-subscription-types
    steps:
      - label: the storage advertises notifications (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: NotificationService
      - label: the service names its endpoint and subscription types
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: NotificationService
                - pointer: /serviceEndpoint
                  jsonType: string
                - pointer: /subscriptionType
                  jsonType: array
                - pointer: /subscriptionType
                  every:
                    - pointer: ""
                      jsonType: string

  - id: "#subscription-create"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: subscription-create
    label: An authenticated lws+json POST to the NotificationService creates a subscription
    comment: >-
      alice subscribes to her test container with the fields 10.3.1 requires (type, one
      of the advertised subscription types, and topic, an array of URIs) plus the inbox a
      WebhookSubscription carries. The response is application/lws+json with type equal
      to the requested type and a subscription URL. The inbox is the storage URI: a
      public HTTPS URL the target will accept as a delivery target, and nothing in the
      topic changes while the subscription lives, so nothing is delivered to it.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#subscriptions
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#subscription-request
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#subscription-response
    traits: [Post, Notifications]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/subscription-create-post-lws-json
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/subscription-request-required-fields
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/subscription-request-type
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/subscription-request-topic
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/subscription-request-additional-fields
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/subscription-response-lws-json
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/subscription-response-type
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/subscription-response-subscription-url
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/notification-suite-subscription-type-identifier
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers webhook subscriptions (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: NotificationService
                - pointer: /subscriptionType
                  hasValue: WebhookSubscription
      - label: subscribe to the test container
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.NotificationService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: WebhookSubscription
            topic: ["${test.container}"]
            inbox: "${storage}"
        response:
          statusCode: "2xx"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          json:
            - pointer: /type
              equals: WebhookSubscription
            - pointer: /subscription
              jsonType: string
              capture: subscription
      - label: cancel the subscription (tidying up, not judged)
        request:
          method: DELETE
          url: "${subscription}"
        response:
          statusCode: ["2xx", "4xx"]

  - id: "#subscription-missing-type-refused"
    type: NegativeTest
    name: subscription-missing-type-refused
    label: A subscription request without a type is refused
    comment: >-
      type is REQUIRED. Without it the server cannot know which subscription suite's
      rules apply, so the request is refused with a client error.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#subscription-request
    traits: [Post, Notifications]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/subscription-request-required-fields
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/subscription-request-type
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers webhook subscriptions (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: NotificationService
                - pointer: /subscriptionType
                  hasValue: WebhookSubscription
      - label: a request with every field but type is refused
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.NotificationService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            topic: ["${test.container}"]
            inbox: "${storage}"
        response:
          statusCode: "4xx"

  - id: "#subscription-unadvertised-type-refused"
    type: NegativeTest
    name: subscription-unadvertised-type-refused
    label: A subscription request whose type the NotificationService does not advertise is refused
    comment: >-
      "The value MUST be one of the types listed in the subscriptionType array of the
      NotificationService." A server that accepted any type would promise deliveries no
      suite defines.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#subscription-request
    traits: [Post, Notifications]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/subscription-request-type
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers webhook subscriptions (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: NotificationService
                - pointer: /subscriptionType
                  hasValue: WebhookSubscription
      - label: a type no NotificationService advertises is refused
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.NotificationService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: TouchstoneUnadvertisedSubscription
            topic: ["${test.container}"]
            inbox: "${storage}"
        response:
          statusCode: "4xx"

  - id: "#subscription-missing-topic-refused"
    type: NegativeTest
    name: subscription-missing-topic-refused
    label: A subscription request without a topic is refused
    comment: >-
      topic is REQUIRED: without it there is nothing to authorize at subscribe time and
      nothing to notify about.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#subscription-request
    traits: [Post, Notifications]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/subscription-request-required-fields
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/subscription-request-topic
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers webhook subscriptions (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: NotificationService
                - pointer: /subscriptionType
                  hasValue: WebhookSubscription
      - label: a request with every field but topic is refused
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.NotificationService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: WebhookSubscription
            inbox: "${storage}"
        response:
          statusCode: "4xx"

  - id: "#subscription-unreadable-topic-refused"
    type: NegativeTest
    name: subscription-unreadable-topic-refused
    label: A subscription naming any resource the subscriber cannot read is refused
    comment: >-
      "If a subscriber does not have the equivalent of read access to all resources listed
      in the topic array, the server MUST reject the subscription request." bob may read
      one resource and nothing else. First, as a control, he may subscribe to that one
      resource: a server that refuses him outright makes the refusals below prove
      nothing, so the test does not apply. Then a topic that adds alice's private test
      container, and one that names only it, are both refused. Otherwise bob would learn
      of changes to resources he cannot read.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#subscription-authorization
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#security-notifications
    traits: [Post, Notifications, Authz, Private]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/subscription-authorization-on-create
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/security-notification-access-control
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: shared
          contentType: text/plain
          body: bob may read this, and only this
          authorization:
            read: [bob]
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers webhook subscriptions (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: NotificationService
                - pointer: /subscriptionType
                  hasValue: WebhookSubscription
      - label: bob may subscribe to the resource he can read (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        as: bob
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.NotificationService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: WebhookSubscription
            topic: ["${shared}"]
            inbox: "${storage}"
        response:
          statusCode: "2xx"
          json:
            - pointer: /subscription
              jsonType: string
              capture: allowed
      - label: cancel that subscription (tidying up, not judged)
        as: bob
        request:
          method: DELETE
          url: "${allowed}"
        response:
          statusCode: ["2xx", "4xx"]
      - label: adding alice's private container to the topic is refused
        as: bob
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.NotificationService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: WebhookSubscription
            topic: ["${shared}", "${test.container}"]
            inbox: "${storage}"
        response:
          statusCode: "4xx"
      - label: and so is a topic naming only that container
        as: bob
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.NotificationService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: WebhookSubscription
            topic: ["${test.container}"]
            inbox: "${storage}"
        response:
          statusCode: "4xx"

  - id: "#subscription-after-revocation-refused"
    type: NegativeTest
    name: subscription-after-revocation-refused
    label: Once a grant is revoked, the agent it named can no longer subscribe to the resource
    comment: >-
      Subscribe-time authorization is decided by access as it is now, not as it was. bob
      is granted read on a resource and may subscribe to it. Once alice revokes the grant
      and bob can no longer read the resource, a new subscription to it is refused. The
      revocation itself is a precondition (access-grant-revoke tests it), so a server whose
      revocation does not take effect makes this test inapplicable, not failed twice.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#subscription-authorization
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#access-requests-and-grants
    traits: [Post, Delete, Notifications, AccessGrants, Authz]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/subscription-authorization-on-create
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/security-notification-access-control
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: shared
          contentType: text/plain
          body: readable by bob until the grant is revoked
    steps:
      - label: the storage offers webhook subscriptions (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: NotificationService
                - pointer: /subscriptionType
                  hasValue: WebhookSubscription
      - label: grant bob read on the resource
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.AccessGrantService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: [AccessGrant]
            storage: "${storage}"
            access:
              - type: [AccessPolicy]
                action: [read]
                assignee: "${identity.bob.webid}"
                target:
                  type: StorageResource
                  value: ["${shared}"]
        response:
          statusCode: 201
          location:
            capture: grant
            cleanup: true
      - label: with the grant, bob may subscribe (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        as: bob
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.NotificationService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: WebhookSubscription
            topic: ["${shared}"]
            inbox: "${storage}"
        response:
          statusCode: "2xx"
          json:
            - pointer: /subscription
              jsonType: string
              capture: granted
      - label: cancel that subscription (tidying up, not judged)
        as: bob
        request:
          method: DELETE
          url: "${granted}"
        response:
          statusCode: ["2xx", "4xx"]
      - label: alice revokes the grant
        request:
          method: DELETE
          url: "${grant}"
        response:
          statusCode: "2xx"
      - label: bob can no longer read the resource (otherwise revocation did not take effect, and this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        as: bob
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${shared}"
        response:
          statusCode: [403, 404]
      - label: a new subscription to it is refused
        as: bob
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.NotificationService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: WebhookSubscription
            topic: ["${shared}"]
            inbox: "${storage}"
        response:
          statusCode: "4xx"
